the PG5, an RV designed to generate and store power while towing and recharge an electric truck afterward. Its unified energy system combines a 43 kWh lithium-iron-phosphate battery, 1.5 kW of solar capacity, regenerative charging during towing, and the fuel-efficient Horizon gas generator. Together, these sources can provide more than 270 kWh of usable energy per cycle, according to Evotrex. The RV supports vehicle-to-load power for tools and campsite equipment, home backup during blackouts, and truck charging through Tesla\u2019s NACS standard, offering 6.6 kW AC or 60 kW DC charging. Evotrex\u2019s Power Calculator estimates off-grid endurance based on conditions and usage. The PG5 includes a queen bed, convertible dinette, shower and toilet, induction cooktop, microwave, refrigerator, and motorized patio deck. Pricing starts at $119,900, while the fully equipped Atlas trim begins at $159,990. The RV weighs 9,500 pounds gross and 8,350 pounds dry. Production is expected in late 2026, with deliveries planned for early 2027.","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":13},"pub_date":1767730826.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/3LWXMArPIn7OJAvZr7FrAeC82fEFWdKg4TyIyrBmVwxD49m2KlzF7eAAUN8htZYBNx8HYVBd9R95OahTFz47lUabU9SM9hrufy9cICPdfy0I-nzHribjXNdE41yXRi3Z6I4sAgEabEi4xqHQz-9AOp5CYXG3-Tw18hh5vpBWTEOWP9ptYEcbtcJfjD6lEE7mP_Z6g6sD4m9GZz1D_IeF09xzkcAXgONsSA9Q27_zKwTJeh98WAsYJhCS5JIz3pd5","attribution":"www.theverge.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.unpluggedwatts.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.unpluggedwatts.com/battery-powered-generator-vs-gas-generator/","title":"Battery Powered Generator vs Gas Generator: Which to Buy","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":4},"pub_date":1792540800.0,"attribution":"www.unpluggedwatts.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.bluettipower.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.bluettipower.com/blogs/power-solution/shore-power-alternatives-camp-off-grid-without-hookups","title":"Off-Grid RV Camping Without Shore Power: Complete 2026 Guide - BLUETTI US","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":5},"pub_date":1778198400.0,"attribution":"www.bluettipower.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"generatorandbackup.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://generatorandbackup.com/generators/dual-fuel/best-dual-fuel-generators-for-rv","title":"Best Dual Fuel Generators for an RV | Generator & Backup","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":6},"pub_date":1791676800.0,"attribution":"generatorandbackup.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"deckedoutrv.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://deckedoutrv.com/best-rv-portable-power","title":"Best RV Generators & Portable Power Stations (2026) | DECKED OUT RV","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":7},"pub_date":null,"attribution":"deckedoutrv.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"apnews.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://apnews.com/article/36257eecaf3e3eaffacc2f600bf8d5b0","title":"Battery bank or generator? How to choose the best backup power for your home during an outage","snippet":"Choosing backup power depends on outage length, household needs and budget. Portable battery banks, usually under $100, are convenient for phones, computers and lights but cannot run major appliances. Fuel-powered portable generators can operate refrigerators, fans and some air conditioners for roughly 6\u201312 hours or longer, but must be used outdoors to prevent carbon-monoxide poisoning; fuel costs, maintenance and limited tank capacity are concerns during prolonged outages. Whole-house generators, typically costing $5,000\u2013$20,000 or more, automatically switch on when grid power fails and may suit homes with frequent outages or essential medical equipment, though installation takes time. Fossil-fuel-free portable power stations, charged from outlets or small solar panels, can run a wider range of devices, with prices from a few hundred dollars to $3,500 or more. Rooftop solar paired with a home battery can replenish stored power during extended outages, but may cost at least $20,000. Some electric vehicles can also supply home power if equipped for it. Experts recommend weighing upfront costs against outage duration, safety, fuel availability and year-round benefits.","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":14},"pub_date":1784034060.0,"attribution":"apnews.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"outdoorpowerstations.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://outdoorpowerstations.com/articles/portable-power-station-vs-gas-generator","title":"Portable Power Station vs Gas Generator: Honest | Outdoor Power Stations","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":8},"pub_date":null,"attribution":"outdoorpowerstations.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"homepowerboss.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://homepowerboss.com/site/portable-power-station-vs-gas-generator-which-backup-should-you-buy/","title":"Portable Power Station vs Gas Generator: Which Backup Should You Buy? \u2014 HomePowerBoss","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":9},"pub_date":1784332800.0,"attribution":"homepowerboss.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.pond.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.pond.com/home/portable-power-station-vs-generator","title":"Portable Power Station vs Generator: Pros and Cons | Pond.com","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":131979,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":10},"pub_date":null,"attribution":"www.pond.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"poweroutlast.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://poweroutlast.com/portable-pow